    shortAnswer: "A business loan provides funding for working capital, equipment, expansion or other business needs. Eligibility, interest and repayment depend on the lender, product and borrower profile.",
    simpleExplanation: ["Business loans may be term loans, working-capital facilities, cash credit, equipment finance or government-linked products. Choose based on what the money is for and how the business will repay it.", "Lenders usually review business vintage, turnover, banking history, credit profile, income, existing obligations, KYC and business records. MUDRA products are designed for eligible micro enterprises under their applicable categories and rules.", "Compare total cost, not only the advertised interest rate. Check processing fees, collateral, prepayment terms, repayment schedule and the Key Facts Statement or equivalent documents."],
